From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:02:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] media: mediatek: Add an MT6878 RAW/YUV engine driver
 for a replayed command queue

EXPERIMENTAL: on the phone the first frame overruns the timing generator
on its first line; no frame is delivered yet.

The register settings of a frame of the RAW/YUV engines are made by a
composer that is not available. The kernel side resets the engines, sets
a handful of fixed values, points the engine at the two command lists,
starts them, switches the viewfinder on and handles the interrupts. This
driver does that part and takes the lists from request dumps that the
user captures on their own device (request_firmware,
titan2/camraw-start.bin for the first request of a stream and
titan2/camraw-frame.bin for the per-frame one). No dump is part of the
kernel.

mtk-camraw-replay.c reads a dump as it is (the 64 KiB command queue
slot, the settings buffer, the image outputs and statistics buffers of
the frame parameters, the sensor input of the configuration parameters).
Every descriptor must write slot or settings values into one of the six
blocks (RAW, RMS and YUV of both halves of a frame split between RAW-A
and RAW-B); every address pair at a DMA port must point into one of the
request's buffers, or the request is refused. The buffers are replaced by
buffers of this driver at their own addresses. Pure data code.

mtk-camraw-drv.c: the video node outside the media graph, power, clocks,
larbs through the M4U, interrupts, side B only with twin=1, and for the
first-frame overrun: clock rates at stream start (cam_mhz), register
snapshots at the first start of frame and the first error, prestart,
apply_delay_us and err_mask switches. Depends on MFD_SYSCON (selecting it
closed a Kconfig dependency loop).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
