+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+/*
+ * MediaTek MT6878 RAW / YUV engine pair driven by a replayed command queue.
+ *
+ * The register settings of a frame of these engines are made by a composer
+ * that is not available. What the kernel side does by itself is small:
+ * reset, a handful of fixed values, pointing the engine at the two command
+ * lists, starting them, switching the viewfinder on, and the interrupts.
+ * This driver does that part and takes the lists from request dumps
+ * captured elsewhere (mtk-camraw-replay.c), placed at its own addresses with
+ * its own buffers. Nothing in the picture can be changed: size, crop,
+ * colour and gains are those of the captured frame, and the sensor has to
+ * run the mode it ran then.
+ *
+ * Two requests are replayed, each always as a whole:
+ *  - the start request (module parameter start_fw), the first request of a
+ *    captured stream: it alone sets up the timing generator, the grab
+ *    window, the time stamp counter and the interrupt enables. It is
+ *    applied once, before the sensor streams, and produces no picture;
+ *  - the per-frame request (frame_fw), a steady request of the same mode,
+ *    applied after every start of frame, alternately from two copies that
+ *    differ only in the picture buffers. The frame number value of each
+ *    copy is replaced by the number of the application.
+ *
+ * The captured lists program both halves of a frame split between RAW-A
+ * and RAW-B (with their RMS and YUV blocks). With twin=1 the second engine
+ * (mediatek,twin) is powered, reset and initialised as well and the lists
+ * are run as captured. With twin=0 (default) the side B descriptors are
+ * left out and only the left part of the picture is expected.
+ *
+ * The video node delivers the two planes of the picture output in one
+ * buffer, copied at the start of the frame after the one that wrote them.
+ * It is not part of a media graph: the sensor and the sensor interface are
+ * set up through the media device of the CAMSV engine of the same CSI port,
+ * and this driver only asks the sensor interface to stream toward its RAW
+ * destination. See debugfs "status" for what was seen.
+ *
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 serlk
+ */
+
